
🚀 Day 18 of #DrGViswanathanChallenge

Today, I solved LeetCode 26 – Remove Duplicates from Sorted Array.

This problem reinforced the power of the Two Pointers technique for in-place array manipulation. Since the array is already sorted, duplicates appear consecutively, making it possible to overwrite them without using any extra space.

💡 Approach: Two Pointers

I used two pointers:

i → Tracks the position of the last unique element.
j → Traverses the array to find the next unique value.

Whenever nums[j] differs from nums[i], I move i forward and place the new unique element at nums[i]. By the end, the first k = i + 1 elements contain all unique values in sorted order.

⏱️ Time Complexity: O(n)
💾 Space Complexity: O(1)

